  <Prose
    title="Terms"
    standfirst="There is no account, no subscription and no service running behind the app, so there is not much to agree to. What there is, is here."
    updated="18 August 2026"
  >
    <h2>What you are getting</h2>
    <p>
      Some Kaizen is a free application you run on your own device. It is open source, licensed
      under the GNU Affero General Public License version 3 or later — see the
      <a href="/legal/licence">licence page</a>. Your rights to use, study, change and share it
      come from that licence, and nothing here reduces them.
    </p>

    <h2>Your data is yours</h2>
    <p>
      Everything you record stays on your device. Nobody else — including the author — has a
      copy, cannot recover one for you, and cannot delete one for you. Backups are your
      responsibility, which is why the app can write one to a file at any time and why
      importing merges rather than overwrites.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Uninstalling the app removes its data.</strong> A device that is lost, wiped or
      replaced takes the record with it unless you exported a backup first.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The software is provided as is, without warranty of any kind, to the extent the law
      allows. It is not a medical, clinical, therapeutic or fitness-advice product, and nothing
      in it is professional advice of any sort. The full disclaimer is sections 15 to 17 of the
      licence.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reminders are delivered by your operating system, not by any service. Android may delay
      or suppress them — battery optimisation, doze, and permission changes all affect this —
      so please do not rely on the app for anything where a missed notification matters.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Because the app runs entirely on your device with no shared service, there is no account
      to suspend and no content to moderate. If you modify and redistribute it, the licence
      governs what you must do; in particular a modified version offered to others over a
      network must offer its source too.
    </p>

    <h2>If a paid service arrives</h2>
    <p>
      Sync and hosted backup are planned and would be paid. They do not exist today, no price
      has been set and no date has been fixed. If they ship, they will have their own terms,
      published before anyone can subscribe, and they will be optional. This page will say so
      when that happens.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes, and getting in touch</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may change as the project does. The date above says when they last did, and
      the history of every version is in the repository. Questions and problems belong in the
      issue tracker at
      <a href="https://github.com/yebt/some-kaizen" rel="noopener">github.com/yebt/some-kaizen</a>.
    </p>
  </Prose>
